    "head_branch": "claude/run-phase-spec-35-6a-vsjri6",
    "head_commit_message": "perf(store): the phases the series bench found slower read the unit view (spec 35 step 6b)\n\nThe bodies snapshot, engage and ScrumNear's foe index read where units stand from\none view of POSITION and LOOSE_AT a store (ScrumReach.STANDING, at_in,\nUnitView.read_once) instead of ScrumReach.at per unit. The march's walk to places\nholds POSITION and BEARING for each squad's pass, so its walkers step through the\nhold. The field's sync reads its routers' ALONG once a squad (route_point_in), and\nthe scattered route_point is gone. The shuffle's free front place reads no store\nstate, and the rout's cold paths touch one router per event: neither is converted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CLKjTdS1GGuKGjNmMvfaKy",
